{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S2 — Cap Docker overlay2 and BuildKit cache with per-generator alarms\n\n## Why\nDocker overlay/image layers and BuildKit cache were major root-volume consumers in the incident. Existing prune logic is reactive and can run without recovering enough space; it does not impose a hard per-generator ceiling.\n\n## What\nConfigure Docker/BuildKit-supported GC ceilings for Docker image/overlay2 accumulation and BuildKit build cache. Use supported Docker/BuildKit APIs/config (`buildkitd.toml` `gc`, `maxUsedSpace`, `minFreeSpace`, `reservedSpace`, or equivalent `docker builder prune --keep-storage` policy), never direct deletion under `/var/lib/docker`. Add separate observability metrics and CloudWatch alarms for Docker overlay/image and BuildKit cache saturation.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: host Docker/BuildKit config, autodeploy prune integration, observability metrics, Terraform alarms, runbook updates, and tests. Out of scope: review scratch volume, journald, `/var/tmp`, and writable-container-layer reaping.\n\n## Grounding\n- Root alarm text names Docker image/build-cache storage: `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:207-215`.\n- Existing reactive prune behavior: `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:132-140`, `:367-384`, `:410-445`.\n- Docker overlay2 docs describe image/container layers under `/var/lib/docker/overlay2` and warn not to manipulate `/var/lib/docker` directly; BuildKit docs define GC cap knobs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Docker/BuildKit configuration imposes explicit upper bounds for build cache and Docker layer/image accumulation.\n- [ ] Existing safe prune behavior is preserved or simplified without deleting tagged rollback images.\n- [ ] Observability publishes separate Docker overlay/image and BuildKit cache usage/cap metrics.\n- [ ] Terraform declares dedicated CloudWatch alarms for Docker overlay/image and BuildKit cache saturation, wired to SNS.\n- [ ] Runbook explains diagnosis/remediation for each Docker generator and forbids direct `/var/lib/docker` deletion.\n- [ ] Targeted tests cover config generation, observability parsing, alarm actions, and rollback-image safety.\n- [ ] Portability criterion: solution uses Docker/BuildKit host config and local script tests; no CI-provider-specific trigger is required."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788376362608438024,"uuid":"39f2a185-5efe-48b2-b0ad-2f850735aa60"}